From 8f4081392be664256015b4b637bd1f1331d0ecf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:39:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add optional ALeRCE forced photometry support

Adds two new keys to predict(), both False by default, so the existing
behavior is unchanged:

- download_forced: query ALeRCE for ZTF and Rubin/LSST forced photometry
  and append it to the saved light curve files.
- include_forced: actually use the forced photometry when fitting and
  classifying. When False, forced points stay in the saved files but are
  removed before FLEET uses the light curve.

Forced photometry is tagged in the existing Source column as
'Alerce-forced' rather than adding a new column, so the light curve file
format is unchanged.

New helpers in transient.py: get_ztf_forced, get_rubin_forced, and
remove_forced. Both query functions return an empty, correctly typed
table on any failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VTRiAoxMxBpsS4cjSGjm4
