From 447bdd610b9d08f12f9ebedb9fbb1282dbf81ecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:39:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix forced photometry quality cut

The isdiffpos cut was rejecting the good data. On ZTF21aaagypx all 46
points that survived the cut landed on epochs with no alert detection,
with magnitudes 20.8 to 29.7 and a median uncertainty of 1.8 mag, while
the real forced measurements, which agree with the alert photometry to
0.001 mag and have half its uncertainty, were all flagged isdiffpos = -1
and thrown away.

Cut on the measurement uncertainty instead, which is what actually
